# "You may choose not to untap this creature during your untap step" (CR 502.3: the active player determines which of their
# permanents untap). Bot1's Old Man of the Sea takes Bot2's Llanowar Elves "for as long as this creature remains tapped and
# ..." (CR 611.2b). In Bot1's next untap step Bot1 is asked and leaves it tapped, so Bot1 still controls the Elves, and has
# since that turn began, so it taps for {G} (CR 302.6). In the untap step after that Bot1 untaps Old Man: the effect's
# duration is over (CR 611.2b), and the Elves is Bot2's again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Old Man of the Sea
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Old Man of the Sea.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {G}
Bot1.Accept
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Tapped = false

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Island; Old Man of the Sea
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves
